WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.870
We're hanging out with Dave
Chappelle, ladies and gentleman.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.971
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.639
-Hey.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.907
-Caught me smoking.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.441
-That's right.
We caught you smoking.

00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:13.713
But, Dave, I remember
when I used to -- I used to --

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.249
I got on the same bill as you

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.484
back in '97, something like that

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.687
at The Improv,
and you used to smoke --

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.288
-I remember that night
very well.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.456
And you killed.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.524
-Yeah, you remember that?
I was like --

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.460
-Yeah, you used to
have the guitar.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.728
I remember the whole thing.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.196
-Yeah, exactly.
I was like, "Man."

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.232
But I remember just watching,
and, you know, all the comics

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.734
would sit around the side
and just watch each other.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.569
We watched all the comics.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:40.240
And smoking was a big part
of your kind of timing.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.643
-It very much is.
I'll show you how it's done.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.445
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:48.147
Nailed it.
-[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:50.483
-That's what I'm talking about.
But then --

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.251
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:55.088
But then I read somewhere

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.156
that you started stand-up
when you were 14.

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.659
Is that possible?
-It was.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.962
My mother -- My mother used to
have to bring me to the clubs,

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:06.666
which was kind of a nightmare,
'cause I was filthy.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.301
'Cause, you know,
when I was young, I just --

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.370
I just thought being dirty
was the way to go.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.738
-Yeah.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:15.174
-But it was a weird
and wonderful experience.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:16.542
I wouldn't trade it
for anything.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.644
It didn't seem crazy to me
at the time, but when I look

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.647
at my kids, I say,
"That was crazy."

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.148
-Yeah.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:25.351
But, the one thing
I do love about you, too,

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:28.254
is you never forget D.C.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.190
You never forget
actually where you came from,

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:34.260
where you started, and when
you won that Mark Twain Prize,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.462
you actually went back
and you did a master class

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.531
for your high school,
with a local high school.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.833
-Oh, my God, yes.
That was the best part of it.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.635
[ Clears throat ] Excuse me.
And by the way, Jimmy,

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.136
I got to tell you
before I tell the story,

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.704
I love you to death.

00:01:45.704 --> 00:01:49.442
Um, I went to Duke Ellington
School of the Arts

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.943
in Washington, D.C.

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.946
And that place changed my life.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.914
It's partially privately funded.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.883
It's a public school,
but the arts program

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.985
is why they always try
to get donations.

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:05.023
And it is one of the best
incubators to hone your talent

00:02:05.023 --> 00:02:07.159
that I've ever witnessed.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:09.562
And Bradley Cooper
and Chris Tucker and Common

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.131
and Erykah Badu and all my
friends who were at the awards,

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.000
the Mark Twain Awards.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.501
[ Applause ]

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.605
Yeah, they all went to
the school with me the next day

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.940
and taught master classes
for the kids.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.775
It was the most beautiful day,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.544
I think, I've ever lived
in my life.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.211
It meant so much to me.

00:02:26.211 --> 00:02:28.047
-That was so cool
for those kids.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.648
-Yeah, those kids are the best.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.150
Matter of fact, there's a bunch
of my buddies from high school

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.751
with me right now.

00:02:32.751 --> 00:02:34.320
I got a whole crowd
right in here.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.488
-Let me see.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.256
-[ Laughter ]
-Wait. What?

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.925
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.693
Oh, come on. That's a first.

00:02:41.693 --> 00:02:44.931
I think you're the first guest
to bring their own crowd.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.832
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.935
-Always doing everything first!
Always doing everything first!

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:53.539
I want to talk to you about your
podcast, "Midnight Miracle."

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.141
-Ooh, yes. Yes, indeed.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:58.010
-It's available now.
It's on Luminary.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:03.516
Talib Kweli and Yasiin Bey
are your co-hosts on this.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.485
-The greatest partners ever.

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:12.391
-Yeah. They are unbelievable.
Yeah. How did this come about?

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:16.028
-We all -- We were all in Ohio,
and there was a tornado,

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:18.030
so we all --
There was like 20 of us --

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.833
We had to hide in my basement.
It was hilarious.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.735
-[ Laughter ]
-Gosh.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.937
And, you know -- you know,
a tornado sounds like

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:27.273
a freight train's coming, but
there's no train tracks here.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.308
We're talking.
It's a little stressful.

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:31.277
And in the middle
of all this stress,

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.013
Mos goes,
"We should do a podcast."

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.248
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:37.984
And we did it. And we did it.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.151
-You just did it. Yeah.

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:40.819
-And doing this podcast

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:43.088
is one of the most favorite
I've ever done in my career.

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:45.558
Just being able to spend time
with my friends

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.492
and laugh about stuff
and reminisce about stuff

00:03:47.492 --> 00:03:49.328
and figure stuff out.

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:50.796
It's been wonderful.

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.865
-How do you describe the show?

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.900
-Well, you know, it's funny.
You keep holding the thing up --

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.771
All these episodes will exist
on vinyl, ultimately.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.306
-What?!

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:03.242
-So it's like --
Yeah, they're gonna be on vinyl.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.743
-Wait. This is a brilliant idea.

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:07.112
-I'm going the other direction.
It's beautiful, man.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:10.049
And we do --
So, they're all like 25 minutes,

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.951
but they're great.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:14.320
I can't even -- I don't even
know how to describe it.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.222
It's like a variety show on wax.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.222 --> 00:04:19.158
But it's --
'Cause it's music, as well.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:22.595
I mean, Black Star
on the second episode,

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:26.365
they debuted a new song, the
first time you've heard from --

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:29.001
-In over two decades,
the first time they recorded

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.803
as Black Star.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.205
-Wow.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.606
-The song is produced by Madlib,

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.708
who is an amazing
hip-hop producer.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:38.777
And you're gonna hear it
on the "Midnight Miracle" first.

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:40.112
It's beautiful.

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:42.048
-I love that you're always
doing it, you're always

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:43.949
pushing the boundaries
and just trying something.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:47.152
Even though it's vinyl,
it's new, in a weird way.

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:49.255
No one's doing this.
I think it's so fun.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.757
You're involved with the
musical performance tonight,

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:56.029
which is our first live
performance since we shut down,

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:59.365
for a crowd, for an audience.
-Oh, man, this is exciting.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:02.368
Shout-out to J.Period, too.
-J.Period.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.571
And Tiffany Gouché
and Black Thought, obviously.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.840
-You know my guy.
Yeah, what up, Black Thought?

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.741
-What up, what up,
what up, what up?

00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:11.243
-They said that you're --

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:14.280
-"I'm cooler than a cooler
inside of a cooler."

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.715
He knows what that means.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:19.819
-You're providing
narration for this,

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:23.255
so tell me
about this collaboration.

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:25.224
-J.Period is, like, the homey.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.925
If you're into mixtapes,

00:05:26.925 --> 00:05:29.761
he got some of the fieriest
mixtapes that come out.

00:05:29.761 --> 00:05:31.296
You know what I mean?

00:05:31.296 --> 00:05:34.533
There was a Tribe Called Quest
mixtape that I was crazy about.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.036
His Lauryn Hill mixtapes.
There's probably a few volumes

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.771
of that -- those are crazy.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.273
So, whenever someone wants
to get a dope mixtape done,

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:42.808
that's the guy to go to.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.444
So me and J.Period met.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:46.244
He's going to be rocking
with us on some things

00:05:46.244 --> 00:05:47.680
on "Midnight Miracle."

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.950
And I'm happy
he's on the show tonight.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.152
And I'm happy Nikki's on
the show. Shout-out to Nikki.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.920
I don't know where she's at,
but give her my love.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.556
-Yeah. Nikki Glaser.
Yeah, yeah, she's on the show.

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:59.725
Exactly. We'll talk more
about the performance.

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:01.927
But, also, we have
another fun bit. Just --

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:03.295
Everyone just stay tuned.

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:05.865
More with Dave Chappelle
when we come back.

